// The Discrete-Event Simulation library, written in Cadenza itself — a port of camshaft/bach as an
// idiomatic Cadenza library over the `Sim` effect (design: implementation/design/DESIGN-discrete-event-
// simulation.md). A simulation is ordinary tasks that `sleep` on a virtual clock a scheduler
// FAST-FORWARDS between events; the scheduler is a `handle Sim` block.
//
// `cdz` reads these well-known top-level defs to build / run / test the project (a def is the manifest).
//   cdz test implementation/des   — run the @test suite
//
// STATUS (2026-07-19): this packages the SINGLE-TASK fast-forward scheduler (delivered + corpus-pinned
// in spec/semantics/27-discrete-event-simulation.sexp), so a consumer (v-music's DES-composed piece)
// IMPORTS it rather than inlining def-sets. A monophonic — or a flattened-to-time-order polyphonic —
// piece plays over this single task. TRUE concurrent-voice tasks await the multi-task run-sim (parked;
// see design §6 increment 4 KNOWN LIMITATION).

def name = "des"

// Library modules — every source file under src/ (a wildcard, so a new module just drops in).
def modules = ["src/*.cdz"]

// The modules whose `@test` definitions form the suite (same-file with their code).
def tests = ["src/*.cdz"]

def exclude = []
